# Volatile log content that must never count as a difference (plan W23).
#
# Applied line-by-line by `stratum-difftest`'s normalizer (src/norm.rs) when
# whole live logs are compared. The BYTE-EXACT corpus channel never uses this
# file: those blocks contain nothing volatile, and normalizing them would
# hide layout bugs.
#
# Grammar, one rule per line:
#   drop /REGEX/               delete every line matching REGEX
#   sub  /REGEX/ REPLACEMENT   replace every match with REPLACEMENT
#
# The committed corpus's banner has its licence lines REDACTED — the goldens
# are public, the licence is not — so the drop rules below must swallow both
# the live shapes and the literal `[redacted]` placeholders. That is tested
# in norm.rs: a redacted banner and a live banner normalize identically.

# --- the banner's licence block, live or redacted --------------------------
drop /^\s*Stata license:/
drop /^\s*Serial number:/
drop /^\s*Licensed to:/
drop /^\s*\[redacted\]\s*$/

# --- timestamps ------------------------------------------------------------
sub /\d{1,2} [A-Z][a-z]{2} \d{4}[, ]+\d{1,2}:\d{2}(:\d{2})?/ <TIMESTAMP>

# --- absolute paths (macOS, Linux, temp dirs) ------------------------------
sub /(\/(Applications|Users|private|tmp|home|var|opt)\/)\S+/ <PATH>

# --- log open\/close trailer lines Stata writes with name and date ---------
drop /^\s*(name|log|opened on|closed on):\s/
